+
+For a multi-root lossless preservation batch, enforce the aggregate compressed
+byte ceiling on each actual write, including gzip close/footer writes. Stage and
+verify every selected archive, fsync its file and staging directory entries, and
+fsync the complete immutable index before removing any expanded original. Admit
+the maximum complete progress-index footprint together with that index before
+the first removal; checking only the first progress row does not bound later rows.
+Refuse a missing staged archive rather than falling back to an uncapped writer.
+Verify internal hardlink inode partitions as well as resolved file bytes: equal
+independent files must remain independent and a hardlink group must stay linked.
+Compare PAX modification times as exact decimal nanoseconds, not rounded floats.
+Preserve a primary archive-write exception when close/footer or postguards also
+fail, recording the secondary failure separately. These guards preserve storage
+bytes and metadata; they do not establish source origin or universal quiescence.
